# Python packages of the Windows port (top-level; requirements-windows.txt is the full lock made from this).
# Decky Loader for Windows runs plugins on its frozen Python 3.14; the on-device engines' workers run on the portable
# Python 3.14 of the same archive. One cp314 set serves both. scripts/build_windows.py installs the lock into
# plugin-dependencies.tar.gz (py_modules/), which Decky Loader downloads with the plugin (package.json remote_binary)
# and main.py extracts into bin/.
# After changing this file, regenerate the lock (every package pinned, with hashes) with:
#   uv pip compile requirements-windows.in --python-platform x86_64-pc-windows-msvc --python-version 3.14
#          --only-binary :all: --generate-hashes -o requirements-windows.txt
